<title>UK: Lehman appoints new foreign exchange economist.</title>
<headline>Lehman appoints new foreign exchange economist.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers has appointed Francis Breedon as foreign exchange economist, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Breedon is joining Lehman from the Bank of England where he worked since 1989, most recently as head of the Financial Market Structure Research Group. He will be based in London and report to global chief economist John Llewellyn.</p>
<p>The appointment is effective from January 2.</p>
<p>-- Astrid Zweynert London newsroom + 44 171 542 7792</p>
